<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<catalogue id="8269-2d5b-d33a-1ffb" name="Early Welsh" revision="6" battleScribeVersion="2.03" authorName="Jono Firth" authorUrl="https://www.greatescapegames.co.uk/uploads/images/wysiwyg/home-shortcuts/coe/darkages/Early_Welsh_June_1st_2012.pdf" library="false" gameSystemId="c749-87c2-0d4a-5e29" gameSystemRevision="12" xmlns="http://www.battlescribe.net/schema/catalogueSchema">
  <readme>This army list covers non-Romanised armies in Britain that emerged out of the shadows following the departure of the Roman army. With the Saxon invasions, many of these kingdoms succumbed but some retreated from England and others continued in the far north.

An Early Welsh army must include a King or Prince and at least two units of Combrogi.</readme>
